* zleak_matchbegin_stfh.sno -- RSP CONSERVATION witness (FINDING-2026-08-09g)
* A plain ref in pattern position (S PAT) sets flat_deep_arrival, which fires
* stfh() in bb_match_begin and with it x86_zclaim(64).  Nothing reclaims that
* carve on the OS-2 legacy-deep-main arm, so rsp marches down 64B per iteration.
* REQUIRED: rc=0, "r: 3000000".  At HEAD this SEGVs (~130k iterations at 8MB).
* A/B: SCRIP_OS_CAP=0 passes -- that is the diagnosis, not the fix.
* This probe is deliberately LONG-RUNNING: the leak is 64B/iteration, so any
* short probe reaches the guard page never.  That is why the 141 suite is blind.
    &TRIM = 1
    &ANCHOR = 0
    S = 'xxxxxxxxxxbbbccccddddaaaaxxxxxxxxxxbbbccccddddaaaa'
    PAT = SPAN('abcd')
    N = 0
LOOP    S PAT                          :F(DONE)
    N = LT(N, 3000000) N + 1           :S(LOOP)
DONE    OUTPUT = "r: " N
END
